## Lean

{{#if view.shared}}
- A result is done only with no `sorry` and a clean `bin/lean-build --axioms <Module> <name>` (e.g. `--axioms Foo.Bar my_theorem`).
- Look up every library name with `bin/lib-find`; never write one from memory. Same before claiming the library lacks something.
- Test a new definition on one case it must accept and one it must reject. Easy wins in a row mean: suspect the statement.
- Build with `bin/lean-build`, not a bare `lake build`. Two failed rounds on an instance problem: revert and log a blocker.

Rules: [docs/discipline/lean.md](docs/discipline/lean.md).
{{/if}}
